From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 08:50:50 -0647
Subject: [PATCH] clk: samsung: zumapro: Keep the HSI2 GPIO bus clocks on too

CMU_HSI2's two GPIO gates, for pinctrl_hsi2ufs (0x2008) and pinctrl_hsi2
(0x2060), are writable and in the same manual mode as PERIC0's: on the
Pixel 9a both CLK_CON_GAT registers read 0x100000 (MANUAL set, CG_VAL
clear), and the clock summary shows them at enable count 0 between pin
controller accesses. So the pin controller turns them on and off around
every access, as it did PERIC0's.

No hang has been seen on these blocks: their lines (the Wi-Fi's PERST#
and WL_REG_ON on gph3, the UFS pins) change rarely. But the PERIC0 hang
followed the gate toggling, not anything specific to that block, and
stock's pin controllers name no clocks, so Google's kernel never gates
any GPIO bus clock. Mark both gates critical as well.

Signed-off-by: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/clk/samsung/clk-zumapro.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/samsung/clk-zumapro.c b/drivers/clk/samsung/clk-zumapro.c
index a2811b7fd..4e47c45c1 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/samsung/clk-zumapro.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/samsung/clk-zumapro.c
@@ -287,10 +287,11 @@ static const struct samsung_gate_clock hsi2_gates[] __initconst = {
 	     0x20d0, 21, CLK_IGNORE_UNUSED, 0),
 	GATE(CLK_GOUT_SYSREG_HSI2, "zumapro_sysreg_hsi2", "zumapro_hsi2_noc_user",
 	     0x20e8, 21, CLK_IGNORE_UNUSED, 0),
+	/* GPIO bus clocks stay on, as for PERIC0's below */
 	GATE(CLK_GOUT_GPIO_HSI2UFS, "zumapro_gpio_hsi2ufs", "zumapro_hsi2_noc_user",
-	     0x2008, 21, CLK_IGNORE_UNUSED, 0),
+	     0x2008, 21, CLK_IS_CRITICAL, 0),
 	GATE(CLK_GOUT_GPIO_HSI2, "zumapro_gpio_hsi2", "zumapro_hsi2_noc_user",
-	     0x2060, 21, CLK_IGNORE_UNUSED, 0),
+	     0x2060, 21, CLK_IS_CRITICAL, 0),
 	GATE(CLK_GOUT_PCIE1_CTL_APB, "zumapro_pcie1_ctl_apb",
 	     "zumapro_hsi2_noc_user", 0x2094, 21, CLK_IGNORE_UNUSED, 0),
 	GATE(CLK_GOUT_PCIE1_DBI_ACLK, "zumapro_pcie1_dbi_aclk",
